# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` Hanya membawa ``docker0`` Setelah daemon berjalan, dan konfigurasi daemon ditulis sebelum itu pada node segar - fakta dikumpulkan pada play start, dan tidak ada lagi yang mengumpulkannya setelah pemasangan. Oleh karena itu, Pembacaan fakta saja tidak menghasilkan apa-apa pada larian yang harus memancarkan alamat, yang meninggalkan wadah dalam menunjuk pada resolver clearnet dan pemeriksaan DIND DNS gagal pada domain hanya node dnsmasq tahu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (default)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (default) balut `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD)MAD berjalan ~70 Sub-roles hulu untuk mengantarkan Synapse, Element, setiap jembatan didukung, Element Call, dan Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus PIN MDAD oleh commit, memberikan inventaris MDAD dari ``services.matrix.*`` Kenop, dan menonaktifkan Traefik / Postgres yang dibundel MDAD / Postgres / Redis Jadi layanan Infinito pusat kembali tumpukan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` Dia adalah publik S3 Titik akhir dan dapat dicapai tanpa SSO ging."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` Kata faksion dibaca dari variabel main kecuali jika diberikan sebagai ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` Nama-nama blok daripada ``ports``, Untuk DiscourseBerkas peluncur yang mana ``expose:`` Daftar adalah apa yang menjadi ``docker run -p`` Di sana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` Dari klien yang melakukan penemuan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Asisten Rumah Meneropong token ke rekening yang dicetak. Pengerahan uang ini untuk administrator, jadi panggilan tiba sebagai administrator siapa pun yang meminta klien. Eksposur radiasi masih terikat jangkauan. Ke server alat digeret pada peran ``mcp`` RBAC group."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Hampir terikat panggilan oleh rekening token milik. Ini merupakan mint pengerahan data pribadi untuk rekening administrator, jadi panggilan tiba dengan hak rekening yang diminta. Mencapai tool server digeret pada peran ``mcp`` RBAC group."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Yang API Token ounza dikeluarkan terhadap akun administrator, sehingga setiap panggilan membawa hak rekening tersebut tidak soal siapa yang meminta klien. Mencapai tool server digeret pada peran ``mcp`` RBAC kelompok, yang merupakan hibah terpisah dari pemberian Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Token akses pribadi adalah minted terhadap ``root`` account dan disimpan di bawah ``administrator`` Kuncinya, sehingga setiap panggilan membawa hak rekening itu tidak soal siapa yang meminta klien. Mencapai tool server digeret pada peran ``mcp`` RBAC kelompok, yang merupakan hibah terpisah dari pemberian GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``:Tanda token layanan web dikeluarkan terhadap akun administrator, sehingga panggilan membawa hak rekening tersebut terlepas dari siapa yang meminta klien. Fungsi-fungsi yang melekat adalah baca-saja, yang membatasi apa yang hak-hak itu dapat lakukan di sini. Mencapai tool server digeret pada peran ``mcp`` RBAC group."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Sebuah panggilan tiba di Baserow Dan hanya mencapai satu ruang kerja yang dimiliki akun. Itu adalah ikatan kedua di bawah daftar nama penyesuaian, bukan pengganti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: KANTOR: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC kelompok, yang merupakan hibah terpisah dari memegang Nextcloud Akun."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: Identitas panggilan MCP dijalankan sebagai. ``user`` Dan ``oidc`` tambahan tambahan membutuhkan ``delegation`` blok, karena pembawa penempatan yang diberikan adalah akun layanan tidak peduli apa klaim metadata."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` Dari data penemuan"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: Skema pengesahan menjaga titik akhir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` Tidak pernah gagal unit - setiap penolakan dilog ke jurnal sebagai ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, Jadi, periksa di sana jika ada host yang kau harapkan tidak. Sebuah pernyataan ``btrfs``/ / / //``zfs`` sebaliknya, yang merupakan titik menyatakannya. Sebelum setiap snapshot peluncur juga menghapus ``.baudolo-*`` Sisa-sisa sisa daun lari mati di dalam akar data."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: KANTOR: ``cloud`` Fiji atau ``chezmoi``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (Perancis): direktori dasar untuk berkas CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` Pre-pembersihan skema di satu sesi psql dan memutar ulang dump di berikutnya, jadi konsumen yang boot di antara penciptaan ulang skema dan replay mati sendiri ``CREATE TABLE``. Oleh karena itu penolakan sementara konsumen naik."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` Di pusat MariaDBNama ``root`` Untuk membuat DB per-site pada penyebaran pertama."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` Hanya pernah ada di dalam EspoCRM Melalui OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` Persona-persona yang dijalankan di setiap varian."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` Dia menyatakan betapa eratnya pasangan peran untuk layanan itu menyatakan: ``>= 1`` Dan pasangan di host yang sama, ``< 1`` Biarkan hidup sendiri. Nilai yang didudukkan pada sisi konsumen dari relasi, sehingga pasangan diarahkan dan dua arah dari satu pasangan tidak perlu setuju."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **orang tua** ``wiki.example.com`` (Amerika Serikat ``example.com`` afex)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` Di mana sys-ca-selfsigned ketentuan akar CA pada tuan rumah. Bekas-sisi-kontainer mengikat-mount target hidup di ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / / / // ``inject_wrapper_container``) Dan mencapai skrip runtime sendiri sebagai env vars dan argumen CLI."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``canonical_domain`` is the host of ``canonical_url``, not the configured domain, so both follow the onion substitution a Tor deployment applies. A consumer that compares it against what a page actually renders would otherwise never match on an onion host."
msgstr "``canonical_domain`` Kau adalah tuan rumah ``canonical_url``, bukan domain yang telah dikonfigurasi, jadi keduanya mengikuti pengganti bawang yang diterapkan Tor. Konsumen yang membandingkannya dengan apa yang sebenarnya diberikan oleh sebuah halaman tidak akan pernah cocok dengan onion host."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: Kata sandi root untuk MariaDB Server."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (Perancis): Path host ke sertifikat Root CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: Apa peran ini dalam audit MCP. Diperlukan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` Dia adalah peta komentar per-kunci yang diurai dari default.env (Lihat :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Kunci dinamis membawa komentar mereka melalui setiap pengendali ``COMMENT`` konstan. ``custom.env`` Pembatalan buang berjalan terakhir (Lihat :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` codex melakukan ulang keluaran statis setiap kali konten yang dikloning berubah, sehingga penyebaran adalah konten-didorong tanpa langkah build runtime apapun."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` and ``pip.conf.j2`` under ``templates/``, and the shell scripts under ``files/``, belong to the development compose stack, which drives them through `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ and `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. The Ansible deployment reads none of them."
msgstr "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` Dan ``pip.conf.j2`` Di bawah ``templates/``, Dan skrip shell di bawah ``files/``, milik dari tumpukan gubah pengembangan, yang mendorong mereka melalui `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ Dan `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. Tugas Ansible membaca tidak satupun dari mereka."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (Andolder)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` Dia adalah orang dalam. Docker Compose tumpuk. Ini tetap dapat dipasang tetapi tidak menerima fitur baru."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` Fiji atau ``swarm`` Untuk pin setiap gambar ke trek itu, ``rotate`` Untuk membagi kedua gambarnya."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` Gagal."

# translation-refused: libretranslate protected-span
# nocheck: url
# translation-rejected: ``config.access_grants: []``\"Administrator-only\"
# daripada publik.
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` Kebijaksanaan adalah keputusan dan hanya mempersempit hasilnya. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` Dan ``tools_unenforceable`` Memaksudkan provider melakukan otorisasi konsumen ini dan koneksi masih tidak dapat dirender, sehingga mereka membatalkan run daripada menghilang diam-diam: klien yang diam-diam berakhir dengan lebih sedikit alat daripada deployment yang dideklarasikan tidak dapat dibedakan dari satu yang bekerja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: Penghapusan opsional"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` Tidak digunakan untuk menghapus sumber daya Docker yang tidak digunakan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` Untuk setiap bahasa tapi bahasa sumber, ``docs`` Bahasa mereka LibreTranslate dukungan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` Dia adalah satu-satunya penolakan yang sah yang tidak dibatalkan, karena penyedia yang mengerahkan kemudian dalam pementasan yang sama belum menulis rahasianya. Pembebasan yang berakhir pada tahap rekonsiliasi, yang berjalan sekali setiap penyedia memiliki: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` Melecehkannya sebagai fatal di sana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
